1
00:00:01,466 --> 00:00:02,467
KATARA: Water...

2
00:00:03,760 --> 00:00:04,928
Earth...

3
00:00:05,762 --> 00:00:06,888
Fire...

4
00:00:07,972 --> 00:00:09,224
Air.

5
00:00:10,099 --> 00:00:13,269
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

6
00:00:14,187 --> 00:00:17,941
Then everything changed
when the fire nation attacked.

7
00:00:18,691 --> 00:00:22,278
Only the Avatar, master of all
four elements, could stop them.

8
00:00:22,695 --> 00:00:25,907
But when the world
needed him most, he vanished.

9
00:00:26,407 --> 00:00:28,785
A hundred years passed and my brother
and I discovered the new Avatar

10
00:00:29,702 --> 00:00:31,871
an airbender named Aang.

11
00:00:31,955 --> 00:00:34,082
And although his airbending
skills are great

12
00:00:34,165 --> 00:00:36,459
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

13
00:00:36,543 --> 00:00:37,544
AANG: Oof!

14
00:00:37,794 --> 00:00:41,422
But I believe Aang
can save the world.

15
00:00:41,548 --> 00:00:43,216
( OPENING MUSIC PLAYING )

16
00:00:47,136 --> 00:00:49,097
MAN: Previously on Avatar.

17
00:00:49,931 --> 00:00:52,559
WOMAN: Ember Island
is a magical place.

18
00:00:53,643 --> 00:00:55,770
TY LEE: Doesn't your family have
a house on Ember Island?

19
00:00:56,020 --> 00:00:58,856
AZULA: We used to come every summer
when we were kids.

20
00:00:59,440 --> 00:01:00,692
ZUKO: That was a long time ago.

21
00:01:01,442 --> 00:01:05,321
WOMAN: Like waves washing away
the footprints on the sand

22
00:01:06,030 --> 00:01:09,450
Ember Island gives everyone a clean slate.

23
00:01:09,993 --> 00:01:12,954
Ember Island reveals the true you.

24
00:01:19,335 --> 00:01:21,129
( BIRDS SQUAWKING )

25
00:01:32,599 --> 00:01:34,767
Doesn't it seem kind of weird
that we're hiding

26
00:01:34,851 --> 00:01:36,436
from the Fire Lord in his own house?

27
00:01:36,769 --> 00:01:40,398
I told you, my father hasn't come here
since our family was actually happy.

28
00:01:41,107 --> 00:01:42,358
And that was a long time ago.

29
00:01:42,650 --> 00:01:44,986
It's the last place anyone
would think to look for us.

30
00:01:45,320 --> 00:01:47,113
You guys are not
gonna believe this.

31
00:01:47,614 --> 00:01:48,990
There's a play about us.

32
00:01:49,657 --> 00:01:51,701
We were just in town,
and we found this poster.

33
00:01:52,243 --> 00:01:53,244
KATARA: What?

34
00:01:53,328 --> 00:01:54,871
How is that possible?

35
00:01:55,079 --> 00:01:56,080
Listen to this.

36
00:01:56,164 --> 00:01:57,832
"The Boy In The Iceberg is
a new production

37
00:01:57,915 --> 00:01:59,834
"from acclaimed playwright Pu-on Tin,

38
00:02:00,043 --> 00:02:02,962
"who scoured the globe, gathering
information on the Avatar.

39
00:02:03,338 --> 00:02:05,965
"From the icy south pole
to the heart of Ba Sing Se.

40
00:02:06,132 --> 00:02:09,010
"His sources include
singing nomads, pirates, prisoners of war

41
00:02:09,093 --> 00:02:11,596
"and a surprisingly knowledgeable
merchant of cabbage."

42
00:02:12,138 --> 00:02:14,599
SUKI: "Brought to you by the critically
acclaimed Ember Island players."

43
00:02:15,391 --> 00:02:16,392
Ugh.

44
00:02:16,684 --> 00:02:18,478
My mother used to
take us to see them.

45
00:02:18,728 --> 00:02:21,314
They butchered Love Amongst
The Dragons every year.

46
00:02:22,523 --> 00:02:24,400
Sokka, do you really think
it's a good idea

47
00:02:24,484 --> 00:02:26,527
for us to attend a play about ourselves?

48
00:02:26,986 --> 00:02:28,446
Come on.
A day at the theater?

49
00:02:28,655 --> 00:02:31,574
This is the kind of wacky,
time-wasting nonsense I've been missing.

50
00:02:35,328 --> 00:02:38,164
( GENERAL CONVERSATIONS )

51
00:02:43,461 --> 00:02:45,963
Hey, uh, I wanted to sit there.

52
00:02:46,297 --> 00:02:47,298
Just sit next to me.

53
00:02:47,382 --> 00:02:48,549
What's the big deal?

54
00:02:48,633 --> 00:02:50,843
I was just... I wanted to...

55
00:02:52,345 --> 00:02:53,596
Okay.

56
00:02:53,971 --> 00:02:56,224
Why are we sitting
in the nosebleed section?

57
00:02:56,391 --> 00:02:58,309
My feet can't see
a thing from up here.

58
00:02:58,476 --> 00:02:59,477
Don't worry.

59
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:01,145
I'll tell your feet
what's happening.

60
00:03:01,813 --> 00:03:03,815
( MUSIC PLAYING )

61
00:03:08,111 --> 00:03:09,237
( GASPING )

62
00:03:10,279 --> 00:03:11,280
( SIGHING )

63
00:03:11,406 --> 00:03:13,199
Sokka, my only brother.

64
00:03:13,574 --> 00:03:16,661
We constantly roam
these icy south pole seas

65
00:03:16,869 --> 00:03:20,206
and yet, never do we find
anything fulfilling.

66
00:03:20,957 --> 00:03:23,501
All I want is a full feeling
in my stomach.

67
00:03:23,584 --> 00:03:24,627
I'm starving.

68
00:03:24,752 --> 00:03:26,421
( LAUGHING )

69
00:03:29,424 --> 00:03:31,801
ACTRESS KATARA: Is food the only
thing on your mind?

70
00:03:32,301 --> 00:03:35,680
Well, I'm trying to get it out
of my mind and into my mouth.

71
00:03:35,972 --> 00:03:37,056
I'm starving.

72
00:03:37,265 --> 00:03:38,266
( AUDIENCE LAUGHING )

73
00:03:38,349 --> 00:03:39,350
This is pathetic.

74
00:03:39,434 --> 00:03:41,352
My jokes are way
funnier than this.

75
00:03:41,477 --> 00:03:42,895
( LAUGHING )

76
00:03:42,979 --> 00:03:45,022
I think he's got you pegged.

77
00:03:45,565 --> 00:03:48,818
ACTRESS KATARA: Every day,
the world awaits a beacon to guide us,

78
00:03:48,985 --> 00:03:50,570
yet none appears.

79
00:03:50,653 --> 00:03:56,534
Still, we cannot give up hope,
for hope is all we have

80
00:03:56,617 --> 00:04:01,539
and we must never relinquish it, even...
Even to our dying breath.

81
00:04:01,748 --> 00:04:03,291
( SOBBING )

82
00:04:04,792 --> 00:04:06,002
Well, that's just silly.

83
00:04:06,085 --> 00:04:07,670
I don't sound like that.

84
00:04:07,795 --> 00:04:09,005
( LAUGHING )

85
00:04:09,088 --> 00:04:11,424
Oh, man, this writer's a genius.

86
00:04:15,928 --> 00:04:20,558
ACTRESS KATARA: It appears to be someone
frozen in ice, perhaps for 100 years.

87
00:04:20,933 --> 00:04:22,143
ACTOR SOKKA: But who?

88
00:04:22,351 --> 00:04:24,520
Who is the boy in the iceberg?

89
00:04:26,022 --> 00:04:27,023
Waterbend!

90
00:04:27,231 --> 00:04:28,232
Hi-ya!

91
00:04:33,696 --> 00:04:35,782
( CROWD "OOH"ING )

92
00:04:36,741 --> 00:04:39,160
Who are you, frozen boy?

93
00:04:39,744 --> 00:04:40,953
( LAUGHING )

94
00:04:41,037 --> 00:04:44,415
I'm the avatar, silly,
here to spread joy and fun.

95
00:04:45,124 --> 00:04:47,502
Wait, is that
a woman playing me?

96
00:04:48,795 --> 00:04:50,463
( GROWLING )

97
00:04:55,802 --> 00:04:56,803
( GASPING )

98
00:04:56,886 --> 00:04:58,471
An airbender.

99
00:04:58,721 --> 00:05:03,100
My heart is so full of hope
that it's making me tear-bend.

100
00:05:03,392 --> 00:05:05,645
( SOBBING )

101
00:05:06,979 --> 00:05:10,483
My stomach is so empty
that it's making me tear-bend.

102
00:05:10,691 --> 00:05:11,943
( SOBBING )

103
00:05:12,652 --> 00:05:13,861
I need meat!

104
00:05:14,153 --> 00:05:15,154
( GASPING )

105
00:05:15,238 --> 00:05:16,447
But wait.

106
00:05:16,531 --> 00:05:18,366
Is that a platter
of meaty dumplings?

107
00:05:18,950 --> 00:05:20,368
ACTOR SOKKA: Oh, where, where?

108
00:05:20,785 --> 00:05:22,495
( LAUGHING )

109
00:05:23,246 --> 00:05:26,165
Did I mention that I'm
an incurable prankster?

110
00:05:27,583 --> 00:05:29,043
I don't do that.

111
00:05:29,335 --> 00:05:30,461
That's not what I'm like.

112
00:05:30,670 --> 00:05:32,421
And I'm not a woman.

113
00:05:33,047 --> 00:05:34,048
( LAUGHING )

114
00:05:34,257 --> 00:05:36,634
Oh, they nailed you, twinkle-toes.

115
00:05:36,717 --> 00:05:37,760
( LAUGHING )

116
00:05:42,265 --> 00:05:44,851
Prince Zuko,
you must try this cake.

117
00:05:45,518 --> 00:05:47,645
I don't have time
to stuff my face.

118
00:05:47,770 --> 00:05:50,398
I must capture the avatar
to regain my honor.

119
00:05:50,940 --> 00:05:55,611
Well, while you do that, maybe
I'll capture another slice.

120
00:05:55,862 --> 00:05:56,904
( MAKING EATING NOISES )

121
00:05:56,988 --> 00:05:58,155
You sicken me.

122
00:05:58,573 --> 00:06:00,658
They make me look totally
stiff and humorless.

123
00:06:01,242 --> 00:06:03,995
Actually, I think
that actor's pretty spot-on.

124
00:06:04,537 --> 00:06:05,663
How could you say that?

125
00:06:06,163 --> 00:06:09,667
Let's forget about the avatar
and get massages.

126
00:06:10,167 --> 00:06:11,961
How could you say that?

127
00:06:18,843 --> 00:06:20,052
Hey, look.

128
00:06:20,136 --> 00:06:21,554
I think I found something.

129
00:06:25,892 --> 00:06:27,768
It's a flying rabbit monkey.

130
00:06:28,269 --> 00:06:30,187
I think I'll name him Momo.

131
00:06:30,396 --> 00:06:31,689
( LAUGHING )

132
00:06:32,690 --> 00:06:33,858
Hi, everybody.

133
00:06:34,066 --> 00:06:35,568
I love you.

134
00:06:36,736 --> 00:06:37,737
Ugh.

135
00:06:42,575 --> 00:06:44,994
Does this dress make
my butt look fat?

136
00:06:45,578 --> 00:06:46,954
( AUDIENCE LAUGHING )

137
00:06:49,457 --> 00:06:54,837
Riddles and challenges must you face
if you are ever to leave this place.

138
00:06:55,755 --> 00:06:57,089
( LAUGHING )

139
00:06:57,673 --> 00:06:58,841
( MOANING )

140
00:07:10,770 --> 00:07:13,481
ACTOR SOKKA: Why did you have to steal
that waterbending scroll?

141
00:07:14,690 --> 00:07:17,485
( SOBBING ): It just gave me
so much hope.

142
00:07:17,693 --> 00:07:19,070
( SOBBING )

143
00:07:23,699 --> 00:07:25,785
The avatar is mine!

144
00:07:25,993 --> 00:07:27,870
Wait, who's coming?

145
00:07:28,454 --> 00:07:32,792
MALE VOICE: I am the blue spirit,
the scourge of the fire nation

146
00:07:32,875 --> 00:07:34,502
Here to save the avatar.

147
00:07:40,967 --> 00:07:42,677
ACTOR AANG: My hero.

148
00:07:52,144 --> 00:07:53,521
( SOBBING )

149
00:07:55,314 --> 00:07:56,857
Don't cry, baby.

150
00:07:57,483 --> 00:08:00,319
Jet will wipe out
that nasty town for you.

151
00:08:05,658 --> 00:08:06,701
ACTRESS KATARA: Oh, Jet.

152
00:08:06,784 --> 00:08:08,285
You're so bad.

153
00:08:09,578 --> 00:08:10,746
( LAUGHING )

154
00:08:11,998 --> 00:08:17,336
Look, it's the great divide, the biggest
canyon in the earth kingdom.

155
00:08:19,588 --> 00:08:21,048
Eh, let's keep flying.

156
00:08:23,300 --> 00:08:24,802
Don't go, Yue.

157
00:08:25,011 --> 00:08:28,139
You're the only woman who's ever
taken my mind off of food.

158
00:08:29,807 --> 00:08:30,808
( GAGS )

159
00:08:30,891 --> 00:08:33,019
Wait. Did you have
pickled fish for dinner?

160
00:08:33,519 --> 00:08:34,729
Goodbye, Sokka.

161
00:08:34,937 --> 00:08:37,523
I have important moon duties
to take care of.

162
00:08:38,524 --> 00:08:41,986
And yes, I did
have pickled fish.

163
00:08:42,486 --> 00:08:43,571
( LAUGHING )

164
00:08:43,738 --> 00:08:45,573
You never told me you made out
with the moon spirit.

165
00:08:45,781 --> 00:08:47,992
Shh, I'm trying to watch.

166
00:08:57,168 --> 00:08:58,377
( LAUGHING )

167
00:08:58,461 --> 00:09:01,172
The avatar is back
to save the day!

168
00:09:01,255 --> 00:09:02,465
Yay!

169
00:09:08,512 --> 00:09:09,722
( CHEERING AND APPLAUSE )

170
00:09:09,805 --> 00:09:10,931
-( GROANING )
-( LAUGHING )

171
00:09:18,481 --> 00:09:21,108
ZUKO: So far, this intermission
is the best part of the play.

172
00:09:21,609 --> 00:09:23,444
Apparently, the playwright
thinks I'm an idiot

173
00:09:23,527 --> 00:09:25,696
who tells bad jokes
about meat all the time.

174
00:09:26,030 --> 00:09:29,283
Yeah, you tell bad jokes
about plenty of other topics.

175
00:09:29,825 --> 00:09:30,951
I know!

176
00:09:31,243 --> 00:09:33,537
AANG: At least the Sokka actor
kind of looks like you.

177
00:09:33,829 --> 00:09:36,373
That woman playing the avatar
doesn't resemble me at all.

178
00:09:36,957 --> 00:09:37,958
I don't know.

179
00:09:38,042 --> 00:09:40,628
You are more in touch with
your feminine side than most guys.

180
00:09:40,878 --> 00:09:41,879
( GROANING )

181
00:09:41,962 --> 00:09:42,963
KATARA: Relax, Aang.

182
00:09:43,047 --> 00:09:44,340
They're not accurate portrayals.

183
00:09:44,840 --> 00:09:47,259
It's not like I'm
a preachy crybaby

184
00:09:47,343 --> 00:09:50,721
who can't resist giving overemotional
speeches about hope all the time.

185
00:09:53,140 --> 00:09:54,141
What?

186
00:09:54,308 --> 00:09:56,268
Yeah, that's not you at all.

187
00:09:56,769 --> 00:09:57,937
Listen, friends.

188
00:09:58,020 --> 00:10:00,397
It's obvious that
the playwright did his research.

189
00:10:00,981 --> 00:10:01,982
I know it must hurt,

190
00:10:02,066 --> 00:10:04,527
but what you're seeing up there
on that stage is the truth.

191
00:10:05,694 --> 00:10:08,656
Well, here we are
in the earth kingdom.

192
00:10:09,323 --> 00:10:13,285
I'd better have a look around to see
if I can find an earthbending teacher.

193
00:10:13,536 --> 00:10:14,578
This is it.

194
00:10:14,703 --> 00:10:16,330
This must be where I come in.

195
00:10:19,750 --> 00:10:21,877
ACTOR AANG: I flew all over town,

196
00:10:21,961 --> 00:10:25,631
but I couldn't find
a single earthbending master.

197
00:10:26,298 --> 00:10:27,341
Here it comes.

198
00:10:27,633 --> 00:10:30,594
You can't find an earthbending
master in the sky.

199
00:10:30,678 --> 00:10:32,346
You have to look underground.

200
00:10:32,721 --> 00:10:33,806
( LAUGHING )

201
00:10:34,265 --> 00:10:35,349
Who are you?

202
00:10:35,891 --> 00:10:40,563
My name's Toph, because it sounds like
tough, and that's just what I am.

203
00:10:40,646 --> 00:10:41,647
( AUDIENCE LAUGHING )

204
00:10:41,730 --> 00:10:42,731
Wait a minute.

205
00:10:42,815 --> 00:10:45,192
I sound like a guy.

206
00:10:45,609 --> 00:10:47,653
A really buff guy.

207
00:10:47,820 --> 00:10:49,947
Well, Toph, what you hear
up there is the truth.

208
00:10:50,322 --> 00:10:51,490
It hurts, doesn't it?

209
00:10:51,699 --> 00:10:52,908
Are you kidding me?

210
00:10:53,033 --> 00:10:54,869
I wouldn't have cast it
any other way.

211
00:10:55,327 --> 00:10:56,412
( LAUGHING )

212
00:10:56,495 --> 00:10:58,080
At least it's not
a flying bald lady.

213
00:11:00,958 --> 00:11:03,294
So, you're blind?

214
00:11:03,794 --> 00:11:04,920
( LAUGHING )

215
00:11:05,171 --> 00:11:06,755
I can see you doing that.

216
00:11:07,006 --> 00:11:10,718
I see everything that you see,
except I don't see like you do.

217
00:11:10,801 --> 00:11:13,012
I release a sonic wave
from my mouth.

218
00:11:14,096 --> 00:11:15,306
( SCREAMING )

219
00:11:20,394 --> 00:11:21,395
There.

220
00:11:21,478 --> 00:11:22,771
I got a pretty good look at you.

221
00:11:22,980 --> 00:11:24,190
( APPLAUSE )

222
00:11:27,443 --> 00:11:31,655
Zuko, it's time we had
a talk about your hair.

223
00:11:31,864 --> 00:11:33,741
It's gone too far.

224
00:11:34,116 --> 00:11:37,411
Maybe it's best if we split up.

225
00:11:41,373 --> 00:11:44,293
ACTOR ZUKO: Azula, my sister,
what are you doing here?

226
00:11:44,668 --> 00:11:45,878
You caught me.

227
00:11:46,128 --> 00:11:47,671
Wait, what's that?

228
00:11:47,963 --> 00:11:49,715
I think it's your honor.

229
00:11:49,924 --> 00:11:51,258
Where?

230
00:11:52,718 --> 00:11:53,928
She escaped.

231
00:11:54,011 --> 00:11:55,054
But how?

232
00:12:00,517 --> 00:12:04,230
If she continues drilling,
this wall will come down for sure.

233
00:12:06,565 --> 00:12:08,609
( LAUGHING ) Yes.

234
00:12:08,734 --> 00:12:10,444
Continue drilling.

235
00:12:10,861 --> 00:12:13,989
The city of Ba Sing Se
can hide no longer.

236
00:12:21,497 --> 00:12:22,706
( YAWNING )

237
00:12:30,547 --> 00:12:31,966
ACTOR AANG: No, Jet.

238
00:12:32,049 --> 00:12:33,634
What did they do to you?

239
00:12:34,218 --> 00:12:37,137
Must serve Earth King.

240
00:12:37,304 --> 00:12:38,389
( GASPING )

241
00:12:39,640 --> 00:12:42,351
Must destroy!

242
00:12:42,977 --> 00:12:44,895
( GRUNTING )

243
00:12:48,023 --> 00:12:50,025
Help. ( GRUNTING )

244
00:12:52,361 --> 00:12:54,405
Did Jet just die?

245
00:12:54,947 --> 00:12:56,782
You know, it was really unclear.

246
00:12:58,075 --> 00:13:02,705
I have to admit, Prince Zuko,
I really find you attractive.

247
00:13:03,205 --> 00:13:04,790
You don't have to
make fun of me.

248
00:13:05,499 --> 00:13:06,834
But I mean it.

249
00:13:07,001 --> 00:13:10,796
I've had eyes for you since
the day you first captured me.

250
00:13:12,798 --> 00:13:13,799
ACTOR ZUKO: Wait.

251
00:13:14,008 --> 00:13:15,968
I thought you were
the avatar's girl.

252
00:13:17,636 --> 00:13:18,637
( LAUGHS )

253
00:13:18,721 --> 00:13:19,722
The avatar?

254
00:13:20,222 --> 00:13:22,308
Why, he's like
a little brother to me.

255
00:13:22,391 --> 00:13:23,392
( LAUGHS )

256
00:13:23,475 --> 00:13:26,312
I certainly don't think of him
in a romantic way.

257
00:13:27,479 --> 00:13:31,317
Besides, how could he ever
find out about this?

258
00:13:33,861 --> 00:13:35,237
Oh, you're getting up?

259
00:13:35,612 --> 00:13:37,698
Can you get me some fire flakes?

260
00:13:39,700 --> 00:13:41,452
Oh, and fire gummies.

261
00:13:42,953 --> 00:13:47,207
Well, my brother,
what's it going to be?

262
00:13:47,416 --> 00:13:50,502
Your nation,
or a life of treachery?

263
00:13:53,380 --> 00:13:54,548
Choose treachery.

264
00:13:54,673 --> 00:13:56,258
It's more fun.

265
00:13:57,926 --> 00:13:59,511
No way.

266
00:14:02,473 --> 00:14:03,766
( GRUNTING )

267
00:14:03,849 --> 00:14:05,225
I hate you, uncle.

268
00:14:05,893 --> 00:14:08,687
You smell, and I hate you
for all time!

269
00:14:12,649 --> 00:14:14,360
You didn't really
say that, did you?

270
00:14:14,735 --> 00:14:16,195
I might as well have.

271
00:14:33,837 --> 00:14:36,090
( APPLAUDING )

272
00:14:37,174 --> 00:14:38,175
Avatar state.

273
00:14:38,258 --> 00:14:39,301
Yip-yip.

274
00:14:48,435 --> 00:14:50,521
Not if my lightning can help it.

275
00:14:52,481 --> 00:14:54,400
( SCREAMING )

276
00:15:00,823 --> 00:15:03,992
The avatar is no more.

277
00:15:05,411 --> 00:15:06,995
( CHEERING AND APPLAUDING )

278
00:15:12,668 --> 00:15:14,336
SUKI: It seems like every time
there's a big battle,

279
00:15:14,420 --> 00:15:15,963
you guys barely make it out alive.

280
00:15:16,213 --> 00:15:17,965
I mean, you guys lose a lot.

281
00:15:18,424 --> 00:15:19,758
You're one to talk, Suki.

282
00:15:19,842 --> 00:15:21,176
Didn't Azula take you captive?

283
00:15:21,427 --> 00:15:22,719
That's right, she did.

284
00:15:24,096 --> 00:15:25,973
Are you trying to get
on my bad side?

285
00:15:26,598 --> 00:15:27,724
I'm just saying.

286
00:15:28,100 --> 00:15:29,393
Does anyone know where Aang is?

287
00:15:29,726 --> 00:15:32,062
He left to get me fire gummies,
like, 10 minutes ago,

288
00:15:32,229 --> 00:15:33,730
and I'm still waiting.

289
00:15:34,731 --> 00:15:35,941
I'm gonna check outside.

290
00:15:46,285 --> 00:15:47,536
Are you all right?

291
00:15:47,703 --> 00:15:49,079
No, I'm not.

292
00:15:49,246 --> 00:15:50,539
I hate this play.

293
00:15:51,665 --> 00:15:54,543
I know it's upsetting, but it
sounds like you're overreacting.

294
00:15:54,877 --> 00:15:56,003
Overreacting?

295
00:15:56,295 --> 00:15:57,796
If I hadn't blocked my chakra,

296
00:15:57,880 --> 00:16:00,132
I'd probably be in
the avatar state right now.

297
00:16:03,385 --> 00:16:04,928
Whee!

298
00:16:06,054 --> 00:16:08,515
Suki, what are the chances
you can get me backstage?

299
00:16:08,765 --> 00:16:10,767
I got some jokes I want
to give to the actor me.

300
00:16:11,101 --> 00:16:16,315
I'm an elite warrior who's trained
for many years in the art of stealth.

301
00:16:17,608 --> 00:16:19,151
I think I could
get you backstage.

302
00:16:21,195 --> 00:16:24,156
Geez, everyone's getting
so upset about their characters.

303
00:16:24,364 --> 00:16:27,534
Even you seem more down than usual,
and that's saying something.

304
00:16:27,910 --> 00:16:28,952
You don't get it.

305
00:16:29,036 --> 00:16:30,245
It's different for you.

306
00:16:30,537 --> 00:16:33,790
You get a muscly version of yourself
taking down 10 bad guys at once

307
00:16:34,041 --> 00:16:35,501
and making sassy remarks.

308
00:16:36,043 --> 00:16:37,753
Yeah, that's pretty great.

309
00:16:37,961 --> 00:16:41,048
But for me, it takes
all the mistakes I've made in my life

310
00:16:41,173 --> 00:16:42,799
and shoves them back in my face.

311
00:16:43,425 --> 00:16:47,429
My uncle, he's always been on my side,
even when things were bad.

312
00:16:47,804 --> 00:16:49,014
He was there for me.

313
00:16:49,431 --> 00:16:52,309
He taught me so much,
and how do I repay him?

314
00:16:52,601 --> 00:16:54,102
With a knife in his back.

315
00:16:54,811 --> 00:16:58,398
It's my greatest regret, and I
may never get to redeem myself.

316
00:16:59,441 --> 00:17:01,485
You have redeemed yourself
to your uncle.

317
00:17:01,902 --> 00:17:04,112
You don't realize it,
but you already have.

318
00:17:04,488 --> 00:17:05,531
How do you know?

319
00:17:05,656 --> 00:17:08,283
Because I once had a long conversation
with the guy

320
00:17:08,450 --> 00:17:10,369
And all he would talk about
was you.

321
00:17:11,078 --> 00:17:12,079
Really?

322
00:17:12,162 --> 00:17:14,081
Yeah, and it was
kind of annoying.

323
00:17:14,540 --> 00:17:15,749
Oh, sorry.

324
00:17:15,832 --> 00:17:17,543
But it was also very sweet.

325
00:17:18,001 --> 00:17:21,672
All your uncle wanted was for you to find
your own path and see the light.

326
00:17:22,172 --> 00:17:23,382
Now you're here with us.

327
00:17:23,966 --> 00:17:25,217
He'd be proud.

328
00:17:26,343 --> 00:17:27,469
Ow.

329
00:17:27,928 --> 00:17:29,221
What was that for?

330
00:17:29,429 --> 00:17:31,014
That's how I show affection.

331
00:17:33,225 --> 00:17:36,645
Your Zuko costume's pretty good,
but your scar's on the wrong side.

332
00:17:38,480 --> 00:17:40,274
The scar's not on
the wrong side!

333
00:17:48,657 --> 00:17:50,075
He's coming this way.

334
00:17:52,119 --> 00:17:53,537
Can I help you?

335
00:17:53,912 --> 00:17:56,081
Actually, I think
I can help you.

336
00:17:56,540 --> 00:17:58,041
I'm a big Sokka fan

337
00:17:58,125 --> 00:18:00,335
but I don't think you're representing him
quite as well as you could be.

338
00:18:00,752 --> 00:18:01,837
Oh, no.

339
00:18:01,920 --> 00:18:03,338
Another fan with ideas.

340
00:18:03,422 --> 00:18:04,548
Just hear me out.

341
00:18:05,257 --> 00:18:07,301
Here's something I think
the real Sokka would say.

342
00:18:07,426 --> 00:18:08,427
( CLEARS THROAT )

343
00:18:08,510 --> 00:18:11,305
What does the cabbage merchant
use to fix his cabbages?

344
00:18:12,014 --> 00:18:13,640
A cabbage patch!

345
00:18:15,058 --> 00:18:16,226
( LAUGHING )

346
00:18:16,310 --> 00:18:17,394
That's actually pretty good.

347
00:18:17,519 --> 00:18:18,604
Let me see those.

348
00:18:20,063 --> 00:18:21,106
( LAUGHING )

349
00:18:21,189 --> 00:18:23,025
A rocky relationship.

350
00:18:23,108 --> 00:18:24,192
Not bad.

351
00:18:24,776 --> 00:18:28,780
Also, don't be afraid to make up some
phrases, especially before an attack.

352
00:18:28,989 --> 00:18:31,867
Something like,
"flying kick-a-pow!"

353
00:18:31,950 --> 00:18:33,452
ACTOR SOKKA: Who are you, anyway?

354
00:18:33,869 --> 00:18:35,579
I'm just a guy who likes comedy.

355
00:18:37,164 --> 00:18:39,499
Katara, did you really mean
what you said in there?

356
00:18:39,958 --> 00:18:41,209
In where?

357
00:18:41,293 --> 00:18:42,753
What are you talking about?

358
00:18:43,045 --> 00:18:46,882
On stage, when you said I was
just like a brother to you

359
00:18:47,257 --> 00:18:48,925
and you didn't have
feelings for me.

360
00:18:49,301 --> 00:18:50,344
I didn't say that.

361
00:18:50,469 --> 00:18:51,511
An actor said that.

362
00:18:52,095 --> 00:18:53,388
But it's true, isn't it?

363
00:18:53,930 --> 00:18:58,685
We kissed at the invasion, and I thought
we were gonna be together, but we're not.

364
00:18:59,436 --> 00:19:02,022
Aang, I don't know.

365
00:19:02,439 --> 00:19:03,690
Why don't you know?

366
00:19:04,024 --> 00:19:05,776
Because we're in
the middle of a war

367
00:19:05,859 --> 00:19:07,903
and we have other things
to worry about.

368
00:19:08,362 --> 00:19:09,780
This isn't the right time.

369
00:19:10,155 --> 00:19:11,865
Well, when is the right time?

370
00:19:12,908 --> 00:19:16,370
Aang, I'm sorry, but right now,
I'm just a little confused.

371
00:19:22,084 --> 00:19:23,794
I just said I was confused.

372
00:19:27,005 --> 00:19:28,340
I'm going inside.

373
00:19:31,218 --> 00:19:33,428
Ugh, I'm such an idiot.

374
00:19:38,975 --> 00:19:40,185
Here's what you missed.

375
00:19:40,352 --> 00:19:43,939
We went to the fire nation, and you got
better, and Katara was the painted lady

376
00:19:44,022 --> 00:19:46,900
and I got a sword,
and I think combustion man died.

377
00:19:47,025 --> 00:19:48,026
Ooh, look.

378
00:19:48,110 --> 00:19:49,611
The invasion's about to start.

379
00:19:49,695 --> 00:19:50,779
Shh.

380
00:19:51,405 --> 00:19:55,409
I just want to let you know,
Aang, that I'll always love you.

381
00:19:56,410 --> 00:19:57,911
Like a brother.

382
00:19:58,286 --> 00:20:01,123
I wouldn't want it
any other way.

383
00:20:11,800 --> 00:20:12,843
Hey, Toph.

384
00:20:12,926 --> 00:20:16,263
Would you say you and Aang
have a rocky relationship?

385
00:20:16,596 --> 00:20:17,597
( LAUGHING )

386
00:20:18,265 --> 00:20:19,391
( GASPING )

387
00:20:19,474 --> 00:20:21,017
I told him to say that.

388
00:20:22,185 --> 00:20:24,604
I hope everyone's ready
for the invasion.

389
00:20:24,980 --> 00:20:25,981
"Slop-a-pow!"

390
00:20:26,314 --> 00:20:27,315
( LAUGHING )

391
00:20:28,233 --> 00:20:30,610
( AUDIENCE LAUGHING )

392
00:20:34,531 --> 00:20:38,660
ACTOR AANG: We finally made it to
the royal palace, but no one's home.

393
00:20:39,244 --> 00:20:40,704
Actually, I'm home.

394
00:20:41,163 --> 00:20:42,539
And I want to join you.

395
00:20:43,790 --> 00:20:45,083
I guess we have no choice.

396
00:20:45,292 --> 00:20:46,334
Come on.

397
00:20:48,670 --> 00:20:49,921
I guess that's it.

398
00:20:50,005 --> 00:20:51,590
The play's caught up
to the present now.

399
00:20:51,715 --> 00:20:52,716
Wait.

400
00:20:52,841 --> 00:20:53,842
The play's not over.

401
00:20:54,134 --> 00:20:58,555
But it is over,
unless this is the future.

402
00:21:01,516 --> 00:21:03,643
With the energy harnessed from that comet,

403
00:21:04,060 --> 00:21:08,190
no one will be able to stop
the fire nation!

404
00:21:08,440 --> 00:21:11,401
Father, Zuko and the avatar
are at the palace.

405
00:21:11,777 --> 00:21:13,487
They are trying to stop you.

406
00:21:14,696 --> 00:21:16,364
You take care of Zuko.

407
00:21:16,531 --> 00:21:19,743
I shall face the avatar myself.

408
00:21:25,290 --> 00:21:27,918
Aang, you find the fire lord.

409
00:21:28,001 --> 00:21:29,419
I'll hold her off.

410
00:21:30,712 --> 00:21:32,964
You are no longer my brother.

411
00:21:33,173 --> 00:21:34,883
You are an enemy.

412
00:21:35,509 --> 00:21:39,346
No, I am the rightful heir
to the throne.

413
00:21:40,514 --> 00:21:42,432
We'll see.

414
00:21:54,569 --> 00:21:56,321
ACTOR ZUKO: Honor!

415
00:21:59,783 --> 00:22:02,202
( CHEERING AND APPLAUDING )

416
00:22:09,417 --> 00:22:13,088
So, you have mastered
all four elements?

417
00:22:13,839 --> 00:22:16,383
Yeah, and now,
you're going down.

418
00:22:17,384 --> 00:22:21,263
No, it is you
who are going down.

419
00:22:21,471 --> 00:22:23,807
You see, you are too late.

420
00:22:24,432 --> 00:22:29,563
The comet is already here,
and I'm unstoppable!

421
00:22:52,043 --> 00:22:53,879
No!

422
00:23:02,762 --> 00:23:04,222
It is over, Father.

423
00:23:04,389 --> 00:23:05,765
We've done it.

424
00:23:05,932 --> 00:23:08,643
Yes, we have done it.

425
00:23:09,185 --> 00:23:15,191
The dreams of my father and
my father's father have now been realized.

426
00:23:15,609 --> 00:23:19,154
The world is mine.

427
00:23:20,405 --> 00:23:22,574
( CHEERING AND APPLAUDING )

428
00:23:29,831 --> 00:23:32,208
ZUKO: That wasn't a good play.

429
00:23:32,500 --> 00:23:33,501
I'll say.

430
00:23:33,585 --> 00:23:34,586
No kidding.

431
00:23:34,669 --> 00:23:35,670
Horrible.

432
00:23:35,754 --> 00:23:36,755
You said it.

433
00:23:36,838 --> 00:23:38,048
But the effects were decent.

434
00:23:48,016 --> 00:23:50,977
( MEN VOCALIZING RHYTHMICALLY )
